{"id":"tq_0238","question":"What gets wetter the more it dries?","answer":"A towel","answer_note":"A towel absorbs moisture as it dries things, becoming wetter itself in the process.","category":"classic riddles","difficulty":"easy","hook":"This one tricks almost everyone the first time..."},
{"id":"tq_0239","question":"A man lives on the 30th floor. Every morning he takes the elevator down to the ground floor to go to work. When he comes back on rainy days he goes to the 30th floor, but on sunny days he can only go to the 15th floor and walks up. Why?","answer":"He is too short to reach the button for the 30th floor — but on rainy days he uses his umbrella to press it","answer_note":"The man is short. He can reach the button for the 15th floor but not the 30th. On rainy days, his umbrella extends his reach.","category":"lateral thinking","difficulty":"hard","hook":"Most people try to think about weather — but it's about height..."},
{"id":"tq_0240","question":"A rooster lays an egg on top of a barn roof. Which way does the egg roll?","answer":"Roosters don't lay eggs","answer_note":"Only hens lay eggs. A rooster cannot lay an egg, so there is no egg to roll.","category":"trick questions","difficulty":"easy","hook":"The trick is hidden in the very first word..."},
{"id":"tq_0241","question":"How much dirt is in a hole that is 3 feet deep, 2 feet long, and 2 feet wide?","answer":"None — it's a hole","answer_note":"A hole has no dirt in it by definition. The dirt was removed to create the hole.","category":"trick questions","difficulty":"easy","hook":"Your brain wants to multiply — but the answer is nothing..."},
{"id":"tq_0242","question":"If you have a bowl with six apples and you take away four, how many apples do you have?","answer":"Four — the ones you took","answer_note":"The question asks how many YOU have, not how many are left in the bowl.","category":"trick questions","difficulty":"easy","hook":"Who said the bowl belongs to you?"},
{"id":"tq_0243","question":"What has cities, but no houses; forests, but no trees; and water, but no fish?","answer":"A map","answer_note":"A map represents these things visually, but contains none of the actual physical objects.","category":"riddles","difficulty":"medium","hook":"Think about representations, not reality..."},
{"id":"tq_0244","question":"Is it legal for a man to marry his widow's sister?","answer":"No — if she's his widow, he's dead","answer_note":"If a woman is someone's widow, that man is dead. A dead man cannot legally marry anyone.","category":"trick questions","difficulty":"medium","hook":"Slow down and read every word carefully..."},
{"id":"tq_0245","question":"Before Mt. Everest was discovered, what was the highest mountain on Earth?","answer":"Mt. Everest — it was still the highest, just not yet discovered","answer_note":"Mt. Everest was always the highest mountain. Discovery has no effect on physical reality.","category":"trick questions","difficulty":"easy","hook":"Did the mountain not exist before we found it?"},
{"id":"tq_0246","question":"A woman shoots her husband, then holds him underwater for five minutes. An hour later they go to dinner. How?","answer":"She's a photographer — she shot his photo and developed it in a darkroom","answer_note":"'Shoot' and 'hold underwater' are photography terms. She photographed him and developed the photo.","category":"lateral thinking","difficulty":"medium","hook":"You assumed the worst — but what if it's all metaphors?"},
{"id":"tq_0247","question":"How many months have 28 days?","answer":"All 12 months","answer_note":"Every month has at least 28 days. The question asks how many HAVE 28 days, not which month has ONLY 28 days.","category":"trick questions","difficulty":"easy","hook":"Think about what 'have 28 days' actually means..."},
{"id":"tq_0248","question":"What can you catch but not throw?","answer":"A cold","answer_note":"You can 'catch' a cold (get sick), but you cannot physically throw a cold at someone.","category":"riddles","difficulty":"easy","hook":"Think outside physical objects..."},
{"id":"tq_0249","question":"A doctor gives you three pills and tells you to take one pill every half hour. How long will the pills last?","answer":"One hour","answer_note":"Pill 1 at 0 minutes, pill 2 at 30 minutes, pill 3 at 60 minutes. Three pills take only one hour.","category":"math tricks","difficulty":"medium","hook":"Count carefully — most people say 1.5 hours..."},
{"id":"tq_0250","question":"What word is spelled incorrectly in every dictionary?","answer":"The word 'incorrectly'","answer_note":"The word 'incorrectly' is always spelled as i-n-c-o-r-r-e-c-t-l-y in every dictionary — because that IS the correct spelling.","category":"wordplay","difficulty":"easy","hook":"The answer is hiding in the question..."},
{"id":"tq_0251","question":"If you're in a race and you pass the person in second place, what place are you in?","answer":"Second place","answer_note":"You passed the person in second place, so you are now in their old position — second place.","category":"trick questions","difficulty":"easy","hook":"You didn't pass first place..."},
{"id":"tq_0252","question":"What has hands but can't clap?","answer":"A clock","answer_note":"A clock has hour and minute hands, but they are mechanical and cannot clap.","category":"riddles","difficulty":"easy","hook":"Hands that never high-five..."},
{"id":"tq_0253","question":"A father and son are in a car accident. The father dies. The son is rushed to hospital. The surgeon says 'I can't operate — this is my son.' How?","answer":"The surgeon is his mother","answer_note":"The classic assumption is that the surgeon is a man, but the surgeon is the boy's mother.","category":"lateral thinking","difficulty":"medium","hook":"Question your first assumption immediately..."},
{"id":"tq_0254","question":"What runs but never walks, has a mouth but never talks, has a head but never weeps, has a bed but never sleeps?","answer":"A river","answer_note":"Rivers run, have mouths (where they meet the sea), have a head (source) and a bed (the riverbed), but none literally.","category":"riddles","difficulty":"medium","hook":"Everything described is a different part of the same thing..."},
{"id":"tq_0255","question":"Some months have 31 days, some have 30 days. How many months have 28 days?","answer":"All of them","answer_note":"All 12 months have at least 28 days. This is the same trick as the previous version.","category":"trick questions","difficulty":"easy","hook":"The trick never gets old..."},
{"id":"tq_0256","question":"What breaks when you say it?","answer":"Silence","answer_note":"As soon as you speak the word 'silence' — or any word — silence is broken.","category":"riddles","difficulty":"easy","hook":"The answer destroys itself the moment you give it..."},
{"id":"tq_0257","question":"You have a match, a candle, a fireplace, and a gas lamp. You only have one match. What do you light first?","answer":"The match","answer_note":"You must light the match before you can light anything else.","category":"trick questions","difficulty":"easy","hook":"The obvious answer is hiding in plain sight..."},
{"id":"tq_0258","question":"A man builds a house with all four sides facing south. A bear walks past. What color is the bear?","answer":"White (polar bear)","answer_note":"A house with all four sides facing south can only exist at the North Pole. The only bears there are polar bears, which are white.","category":"lateral thinking","difficulty":"hard","hook":"Geometry reveals the geography..."},
{"id":"tq_0259","question":"What word becomes shorter when you add two letters to it?","answer":"'Short' — add 'er' to make 'shorter'","answer_note":"Adding 'er' to 'short' makes the word 'shorter,' which literally means more short.","category":"wordplay","difficulty":"medium","hook":"The word describes what adding letters does to it..."},
{"id":"tq_0260","question":"In a year, some months have 30 days and some have 31. Which months have 28 days?","answer":"All of them","answer_note":"Every single month has at least 28 days. The trick is the word 'have' vs 'only have.'","category":"trick questions","difficulty":"easy","hook":"This question has fooled billions of people..."},
{"id":"tq_0261","question":"If there are three apples and you take away two, how many apples do you have?","answer":"Two — the ones you took","answer_note":"You took two apples. You have two apples. The question asks what YOU have, not what's left.","category":"trick questions","difficulty":"easy","hook":"Keep track of who 'you' are in the question..."},
{"id":"tq_0262","question":"What can you hold in your left hand but not in your right?","answer":"Your right hand (or right elbow)","answer_note":"You can hold your right hand with your left hand, but you cannot hold your right hand with itself.","category":"trick questions","difficulty":"easy","hook":"Think about what's physically impossible..."},
{"id":"tq_0263","question":"How far can a dog run into the woods?","answer":"Halfway — after that it's running out of the woods","answer_note":"At the exact midpoint of the woods, every additional step takes the dog closer to the other side.","category":"lateral thinking","difficulty":"easy","hook":"Think about the midpoint..."},
{"id":"tq_0264","question":"I have two coins totaling 30 cents. One of them is not a nickel. What are the two coins?","answer":"A quarter and a nickel","answer_note":"One coin is a quarter and one is a nickel. The riddle says 'one is not a nickel' — the OTHER one is.","category":"trick questions","difficulty":"medium","hook":"Read the clue very carefully — it says ONE of them..."},
{"id":"tq_0265","question":"What has one eye but cannot see?","answer":"A needle","answer_note":"A sewing needle has a 'hole' called the eye through which thread is passed — but it cannot see.","category":"riddles","difficulty":"easy","hook":"A very small feature gives it its name..."},
{"id":"tq_0266","question":"A man walks into a bar and asks for a glass of water. The bartender pulls out a gun and points it at him. The man says 'thank you' and walks out. Why?","answer":"The man had hiccups — the scare cured them","answer_note":"The man had hiccups and needed a fright or a glass of water to cure them. The bartender chose fright — it worked.","category":"lateral thinking","difficulty":"medium","hook":"Why would someone thank someone who pointed a gun at them?"},
{"id":"tq_0267","question":"What comes once in a minute, twice in a moment, but never in a thousand years?","answer":"The letter M","answer_note":"'Minute' has one M, 'moment' has two M's, and 'thousand years' has none.","category":"wordplay","difficulty":"medium","hook":"Stop thinking about time — think about letters..."},
{"id":"tq_0268","question":"What is always in front of you but can't be seen?","answer":"The future","answer_note":"The future is always ahead of you, but it cannot be seen or observed directly.","category":"riddles","difficulty":"easy","hook":"It's coming, but you can never look at it..."},
{"id":"tq_0269","question":"If two's company and three's a crowd, what are four and five?","answer":"Nine (4 + 5 = 9)","answer_note":"The trick is to do the math: four and five added together equals nine.","category":"trick questions","difficulty":"easy","hook":"Most people answer with a social saying — not arithmetic..."},
{"id":"tq_0270","question":"How many bricks does it take to complete a brick building?","answer":"One — the last one","answer_note":"A building is 'completed' with the final brick. Only one brick completes it; all others are just building it.","category":"trick questions","difficulty":"medium","hook":"What does 'complete' actually mean here?"},
{"id":"tq_0271","question":"What are the next three letters in this sequence: O, T, T, F, F, S, S, ?","answer":"E, N, T","answer_note":"The letters are the first letters of One, Two, Three, Four, Five, Six, Seven — so next are Eight, Nine, Ten.","category":"patterns","difficulty":"hard","hook":"Numbers are hiding in plain sight..."},
{"id":"tq_0272","question":"A truck driver is going the wrong way down a one-way street. A police officer sees him but does nothing. Why?","answer":"The truck driver is walking, not driving","answer_note":"The driver is on foot, not in the truck. Walking on a one-way street is perfectly legal.","category":"lateral thinking","difficulty":"easy","hook":"The job title is a trick — not the mode of transport..."},
{"id":"tq_0273","question":"What has teeth but cannot bite?","answer":"A comb (or a saw, or a zipper)","answer_note":"Combs, saws, and zippers all have teeth but cannot bite in the animal sense.","category":"riddles","difficulty":"easy","hook":"Teeth everywhere — but no mouth..."},
{"id":"tq_0274","question":"If you drop a yellow hat in the Red Sea, what does it become?","answer":"Wet","answer_note":"The hat becomes wet when dropped in any sea. The colors in the question are distractions.","category":"trick questions","difficulty":"easy","hook":"The colors are a distraction..."},
{"id":"tq_0275","question":"What can travel around the world while staying in a corner?","answer":"A postage stamp","answer_note":"A postage stamp stays in the corner of an envelope while the letter travels the world.","category":"riddles","difficulty":"medium","hook":"It travels without moving..."},
{"id":"tq_0276","question":"I am not alive, but I grow. I don't have lungs, but I need air. What am I?","answer":"Fire","answer_note":"Fire grows as it spreads, needs oxygen (air) to burn, but is not a living organism.","category":"riddles","difficulty":"easy","hook":"Alive in every way except technically..."},
{"id":"tq_0277","question":"What is the question you can never say 'yes' to honestly?","answer":"'Are you asleep?' (or 'Are you dead?')","answer_note":"If you can answer the question, you're not asleep. Saying 'yes' honestly is impossible.","category":"logic","difficulty":"medium","hook":"The honest answer makes the question untrue..."},
{"id":"tq_0278","question":"How can you throw a ball so it goes a short distance, comes to a complete stop, then reverses direction and returns to you — without hitting a wall or any other object, and without attaching anything to it?","answer":"Throw it straight up in the air","answer_note":"Throwing a ball upward makes it slow, stop, and return due to gravity — no walls or strings needed.","category":"physics tricks","difficulty":"medium","hook":"Gravity is the secret partner..."},
{"id":"tq_0279","question":"What gets bigger the more you take away from it?","answer":"A hole","answer_note":"The more material you remove, the larger the hole becomes.","category":"riddles","difficulty":"easy","hook":"Taking away makes it grow..."},
{"id":"tq_0280","question":"A woman had two sons born at the same hour of the same day of the same year. But they were not twins. How?","answer":"They were two of a set of triplets (or more)","answer_note":"If three or more babies are born together, any two of them share birth details without being called 'twins.'","category":"lateral thinking","difficulty":"medium","hook":"Twins is just one possibility..."},
{"id":"tq_0281","question":"An electric train is traveling north. The wind is blowing east. Which direction does the smoke blow?","answer":"Electric trains don't produce smoke","answer_note":"Electric trains have no combustion engine and produce no smoke at all.","category":"trick questions","difficulty":"easy","hook":"The trick is in the type of train..."},
{"id":"tq_0282","question":"What has four legs in the morning, two at noon, and three in the evening?","answer":"A human","answer_note":"This is the riddle of the Sphinx: a baby crawls on all fours, an adult walks on two legs, and an elder uses a cane (three legs).","category":"classic riddles","difficulty":"medium","hook":"The most famous riddle in all of history..."},
{"id":"tq_0283","question":"How can a man go eight days without sleep?","answer":"He sleeps at night","answer_note":"The man sleeps at night — he goes eight days without sleep, not eight days without sleeping.","category":"trick questions","difficulty":"easy","hook":"Days and nights are different things..."},
{"id":"tq_0284","question":"What is at the end of a rainbow?","answer":"The letter W","answer_note":"The letter W is the last letter of the word 'rainbow.'","category":"wordplay","difficulty":"easy","hook":"Think about the word, not the phenomenon..."},
{"id":"tq_0285","question":"Three men are in a boat with four cigarettes but no lighter. How do they get to smoke?","answer":"They throw one cigarette overboard, making the boat a cigarette lighter","answer_note":"'Cigarette lighter' — throwing one out makes the remaining boat hold a 'lighter' amount of cigarettes — a pun.","category":"wordplay","difficulty":"hard","hook":"This is a pun puzzle — not a survival puzzle..."},
{"id":"tq_0286","question":"What has a bottom at the top?","answer":"Your legs (the bottom of your torso is at the top of your legs)","answer_note":"The 'bottom' (backside) is at the top of your legs.","category":"trick questions","difficulty":"medium","hook":"Think anatomy..."},
{"id":"tq_0287","question":"What do you call a bear with no teeth?","answer":"A gummy bear","answer_note":"Without teeth, a bear is 'gummy' — like a gummy bear candy.","category":"wordplay","difficulty":"easy","hook":"Pure wordplay..."},
