{"id":"tq_0291","question":"If a plane crashes on the border of France and Germany, where do they bury the survivors?","answer":"You don't bury survivors — they're alive","answer_note":"Survivors of a plane crash are alive and do not need to be buried.","category":"trick questions","difficulty":"easy","hook":"The key word is hiding in plain sight..."},
{"id":"tq_0292","question":"What starts with E, ends with E, and contains only one letter?","answer":"An envelope","answer_note":"An envelope starts with E, ends with E, and typically contains one letter (piece of mail).","category":"wordplay","difficulty":"medium","hook":"Think about what the word holds, not just spells..."},
{"id":"tq_0293","question":"A man is found dead in a locked room with 53 bicycles. What happened?","answer":"He was cheating at cards — 53 cards means he had an extra card in his deck","answer_note":"A standard deck has 52 cards. 'Bicycles' are a brand of playing cards. He was caught cheating with an extra card.","category":"lateral thinking","difficulty":"hard","hook":"Bicycle is a brand of playing cards..."},
{"id":"tq_0294","question":"I speak without a mouth and hear without ears. I have no body but come alive with wind. What am I?","answer":"An echo","answer_note":"An echo 'speaks' (reflects sound) and 'hears' (receives sound) with no physical body.","category":"riddles","difficulty":"medium","hook":"Sound without a source..."},
{"id":"tq_0295","question":"What five-letter word becomes shorter when you add two letters to it?","answer":"Short — add 'er' to make 'shorter'","answer_note":"The five-letter word 'short' becomes 'shorter' (seven letters) which literally means more short.","category":"wordplay","difficulty":"easy","hook":"Longer in length, shorter in meaning..."},
{"id":"tq_0296","question":"What room do ghosts avoid?","answer":"The living room","answer_note":"Ghosts are not living — so they'd avoid the 'living' room.","category":"wordplay","difficulty":"easy","hook":"Think about what the room is named for..."},
{"id":"tq_0297","question":"What is so fragile that saying its name breaks it?","answer":"Silence","answer_note":"The moment you say the word 'silence,' silence is broken.","category":"riddles","difficulty":"easy","hook":"The very act of answering destroys it..."},
{"id":"tq_0298","question":"If a red house is made of red bricks and a blue house is made of blue bricks, what is a greenhouse made of?","answer":"Glass","answer_note":"Greenhouses are made of glass — they are called 'green' because they grow plants, not because of green material.","category":"trick questions","difficulty":"easy","hook":"The pattern breaks at the last step..."},
{"id":"tq_0299","question":"Johnny's mother has three children. The first is named April, the second is named May. What is the name of the third child?","answer":"Johnny","answer_note":"The riddle says 'Johnny's mother' — Johnny is the third child.","category":"trick questions","difficulty":"easy","hook":"The answer is the first word of the question..."},
