{"id":"tq_0312","question":"If you had only one match and entered a room with a lamp, a fireplace, and a gas stove — what do you light first?","answer":"The match","answer_note":"You cannot light anything with an unlit match. You light the match first.","category":"trick questions","difficulty":"easy","hook":"First things first..."},
{"id":"tq_0313","question":"What word contains all 26 letters?","answer":"The alphabet","answer_note":"The word 'alphabet' doesn't contain all 26 — but 'the alphabet' as a concept contains all 26 letters. Also: pangram sentences like 'The quick brown fox...'","category":"wordplay","difficulty":"medium","hook":"Think about the concept, not just the word itself..."},
{"id":"tq_0314","question":"What has a head, a tail, is brown, and has no legs?","answer":"A penny","answer_note":"A coin has a 'head' side and a 'tail' side, is copper-brown, and has no legs.","category":"riddles","difficulty":"easy","hook":"Think currency, not creature..."},
{"id":"tq_0315","question":"How many seconds are in a year?","answer":"12 — January 2nd, February 2nd, March 2nd... (the 2nd of each month)","answer_note":"Trick answer: there are 12 'seconds' (2nd days) in a year, one per month. Literal answer: 31,536,000 seconds.","category":"wordplay","difficulty":"hard","hook":"Depends entirely on what 'seconds' means..."},
