{"id":"tq_0319","question":"A clerk at a butcher shop stands 5'10\" tall. What does he weigh?","answer":"Meat","answer_note":"A butcher weighs (measures the weight of) meat — that is literally his job.","category":"trick questions","difficulty":"easy","hook":"His job title tells you the answer..."},
{"id":"tq_0320","question":"David's father has three sons: Snap, Crackle, and...?","answer":"David","answer_note":"The question says 'David's father' — David is one of his sons.","category":"trick questions","difficulty":"easy","hook":"The name is in the question..."},
{"id":"tq_0321","question":"What occurs once in every minute, twice in every moment, yet never in a thousand years?","answer":"The letter M","answer_note":"M appears once in 'minute,' twice in 'moment,' and zero times in 'a thousand years.'","category":"wordplay","difficulty":"medium","hook":"Not time — letters..."},
{"id":"tq_0322","question":"How can you physically stand behind your father while he stands behind you?","answer":"Stand back to back","answer_note":"If you both face opposite directions and stand back to back, each person is 'behind' the other simultaneously.","category":"lateral thinking","difficulty":"medium","hook":"Direction matters more than position..."},
{"id":"tq_0323","question":"What can you add to a barrel to make it lighter?","answer":"A hole","answer_note":"A hole in a barrel allows contents to drain out, making the barrel lighter. Also, removing the plug removes weight.","category":"trick questions","difficulty":"easy","hook":"Remove something to add a hole — it lightens everything..."},
{"id":"tq_0324","question":"What gets more wet as it dries more things?","answer":"A towel or a sponge","answer_note":"As a towel or sponge dries things, it absorbs moisture, becoming wetter itself.","category":"riddles","difficulty":"easy","hook":"Drying by getting wet..."},
